{"strongs": "H3335", "word": "יָצַר", "translit": "ya.tsar", "root": "יצר", "morph": "H:V", "pos": "verb", "gloss": "form, fashion", "definition": "יָצַר verb form, fashion (Late Hebrew in participle יוֺצֵר potter, creator , and derivatives; Phoenician יצר potter ; ᵑ7 יצר Syriac = יֵצֶר etc.; Arabic covenant, contract ; Assyrian êƒêru, as Hebrew, Dl HWB 309 ) — Qal Perfect ׳ י Isa 44:10 יָצָ֑ר Gen 2:8 suffix יְצָרָהּ Isa 45:18 2 masculine יָצַרְתָּ Ps 104:26 + 8 t. Perfect; Imperfect 3 masculine וַיִּ֫יצֶר Gen 2:7 וַיִּ֫צֶר v Gen 2:19 suffix יִצְּרֵהוּ Isa 44:12 1 singular suffix אֶצֳּו֯רְךָ Jer 1:5 Participle יוֺצֵר Isa 41:25 + 20 t.; יֹצֵר Isa 45:18 + 6 t.; suffix יֹצְרִי Isa 49:5 + 11 t. suffix; plural יוֺצְרִים Isa 30:14 ; 1Chr 4:23 construct יֹצְרֵי Isa 44:9 — 1. of human activity: \\ \\ a. of a potter who forms out of clay a vessel Isa 29:16 ; Isa 41:25 ; Jer 18:4 (twice in verse); Jer 18:6 (twice in verse); 1Chr 4:23 ; Lam 4:2 ; Zech 11:13 (twice in verse) (these last two according to Thes SS et al. error for אוֺצָר ); ׳ כְּלִי (ה)י potter's vessel 2Sam 17:28 ; Ps 2:9 ; Jer 19:11 ׳ חֹמֶר הי potter's clay Isa 29:16 ׳ נֵבֶל י Isa 30:14 ׳ בַּקְבֻּק י Jer 19:1 ׳ בית הי Jer 18:2 ; Jer 18:3 . \\ \\ b. of a carver of wood, graven images Isa 44:9 ; Isa 44:10 ; Isa 44:12 ; Hab 2:18 (twice in verse). \\ \\ c. frame, devise in the mind עָמָל ׳ י Ps 94:20 . 2. of divine activity: \\ \\ a. (as a potter) forming Adam out of עפר from אדמה Gen 2:7 ; Gen 2:8 ( J ), beasts and birds, also from אדמה v Gen 2:19 ( J ); Israel as a people Isa 27:11 ; Isa 43:1 ; Isa 43:21 ; Isa 44:21 ; Isa 45:9 (twice in verse); Isa 45:11 ; Isa 64:7 , even from the womb Isa 44:2 ; Isa 44:24 the servant of Yahweh from the womb Isa 49:5 of the formation of the individual man Isa 43:7 Jeremiah in the womb Jer 1:5 the eye of man Ps 94:9 the locust Amos 7:1 Leviathan Ps 104:26 the dry land Ps 95:5 the earth Isa 45:18 (twice in verse); the mountains Amos 4:13 הַכֹּל Jer 10:16 = Jer 51:19 . Figurative perhaps lost sight of in some of the above, and quite certainly in the forming of light Isa 45:7 , of summer and winter Ps 74:17 , the רוּחַ of man Zech 12:1 , and the לב of men Ps 33:15 . \\ \\ b. figurative for frame, pre-ordain, plan (in divine purpose), of a situation מֵרָחוֺק Isa 22:11 of an occurrence מִימֵי קֶדֶם Isa 37:26 = 2Kgs 19:25 יָצַרְתִּי אַף אֶעֱשֶׂנָּה I have planned, I will also do it 2Kgs 46:11 רעה על ׳ י Jer 18:11 לַהֲכִינָהּ ׳ י devised it to establish it Jer 33:2 . Niph`al Perfect לְפָנַי לֹאנֿוֺצַר אֵל Isa 43:10 before me a god was not formed (created). Pu`al Perfect יָמִים יצָֻּ֑רוּ days (that) were pre-ordained (in the divine purpose) Ps 139:16 (compare Qal, 2 b ). Hoph`al Imperfect כָּלכְּֿלִי יוּצַר עָלַיִךְ לֹא יִצְלָ֑ח Isa 54:17 any weapon that is formed against thee will not prosper .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3675')\">BDB3675</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H3335')\">H3335</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3674')\">BDB3674</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3676')\">BDB3676</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>יָצַר</bdbheb> <b>verb</b> <highlightword>form, fashion</highlightword> (Late Hebrew in participle <bdbheb>יוֺצֵר</bdbheb> <highlight>potter, creator</highlight>, and derivatives; Phoenician <bdbheb>יצר</bdbheb> <highlight>potter</highlight>; <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Tg')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵑ7</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <bdbheb>יצר</bdbheb> Syriac <placeholder2277/> = <bdbheb>יֵצֶר</bdbheb> etc.; Arabic <placeholder2278/> <highlight>covenant, contract</highlight>; Assyrian <transliteration><highlight>êƒêru,</highlight></transliteration> as Hebrew, <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Dl')\">Dl<sup>HWB 309</sup></lookup>) — <div class=\"point\"><b>Qal</b> <highlight>Perfect</highlight> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>י</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 44:10\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"44\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"44\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(23,44,10)\">Isa 44:10</ref> <bdbheb>יָצָ֑ר</bdbheb> <ref ref=